From 109f1f1ecb71223dc6005de10b2a5643866fb19d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:48:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(appindexer): share one list of installed apps across the
 panel

the menu's app index, the icon tasklist's matcher and the autostart page
each called g_app_info_get_all() on their own, and every call reads and
parses every desktop file on the system. the matcher did it once per app
it had to match, so at startup the tasklist ran several full scans back to
back on the main thread before its icons showed up.

AppInfoStore now loads the list once, hands the same DesktopAppInfo objects
to every consumer in the order gio lists them, and reloads when the
installed apps change. the app index refreshes from the store's changed
signal and keeps its existing delay.

in testing, with 281 desktop files installed, measured over the panel's
first 90 seconds:

- startup went from nine full scans to one, removing about 180ms of
  back to back main-thread work before the tasklist filled in.
- the panel's user-space cpu time dropped by about a third, from roughly
  410ms to 260ms. most of that was the tasklist's first population, which
  went from about 110ms to 15ms.
- allocations dropped by about a third, from 2.76M to 1.76M, and
  short-lived allocations by more than half, from 522k to 213k.
- peak heap went up by about 0.8MB, since the store keeps the list for
  the life of the process.

windows that fall back to the matcher after startup, and opening the
autostart page, now read the same list, where each used to rescan every
desktop file.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5[1m]
Signed-off-by: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
